  '8.5': { kind: "choice", q: "What happens when this code runs?", code: ["val r = Result.failure<Int>(IllegalStateException(\"closed\"))", "println(r.getOrThrow())"], options: ["It throws IllegalStateException(\"closed\") and prints nothing.", "It prints null.", "It prints 0.", "It prints closed."], exp: "`getOrThrow()` rethrows the stored `Throwable` of a failed `Result`, so `println` never runs. It does not return `null` or a default value." },
  '8.6': { kind: "out", q: "What does this code print?", exp: "`getOrElse` runs its lambda for a failed `Result` and returns the lambda value, so `9` prints." },
